.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt FC-VALIDATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fc-validate
.Nd validate font files
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     fc-validate [ -Vhv ]

      [  [ -i index ]  [ --index index ]  ]  [  [ -l lang ]  [ --lang lang ]
     ]  [ --verbose ]  [ --version ]  [ --help ]  font-file...
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     fc-validate validates font-file(s) if each fonts satisfies the language
     coverage according to the orthography files in fontconfig.  If --index is
     given, only one face of each file is validated, otherwise all faces are
     validated.
.Ed
.Ss "OPTIONS"
.Bd -literal
     This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long options
     starting with two dashes (`-'). A summary of options is included below.

     -i     Only query face indexed index of each file.

     -l     Set lang as a language instead of current locale. this is used for
            -m.

     -v     Show more detailed information.

     -V     Show version of the program and exit.

     -h     Show summary of options.

     font-file
            Query font-file for font faces.
.Ed
.Ss "RETURN CODES"
.Bd -literal
     fc-validate returns error code 0 for successful parsing, or 1 if any
     errors occurred or if at least one font face could not be opened.
.Ed
